.TH FIRESTAFF 1 "2026-07-08" "Firestaff" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
firestaff \- source-faithful Dungeon Master engine for modern hardware
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B firestaff
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIGAME\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Firestaff
is a source-faithful engine for Dungeon Master, Chaos Strikes Back,
Dungeon Master II: Skullkeep, Dungeon Master Nexus, and Theron's Quest.
.PP
Original game data is not included. Users must provide their own legally
obtained game files. Firestaff scans game data recursively by content hash,
so supported files do not need exact original filenames.
.SH GAMES
.TP
.B dm1
Dungeon Master.
.TP
.B csb
Chaos Strikes Back.
.TP
.B dm2
Dungeon Master II: Skullkeep.
.TP
.B nexus
Dungeon Master Nexus.
.TP
.B theron
Theron's Quest.
.PP
Games may be selected either positionally, for example
.BR "firestaff dm1" ,
or with
.BR "--game " .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--duration " ms
Run for the specified number of milliseconds. Use
.B -1
to run until exit, or
.B 0
for one frame.
.TP
.BI "--width " px
Set window width.
.TP
.BI "--height " px
Set window height.
.TP
.BI "--scale-mode " n
Set graphics mode:
.B 1
for original/V1,
.B 2
for enhanced/upscaled V2.1, or
.B 3
for modern V2.2 presentation.
.TP
.BI "--script " cmds
Run a comma-separated input script. Supported public tokens are
.BR up ,
.BR down ,
.BR left ,
.BR right ,
.BR enter ,
.BR action ,
and
.BR esc .
Boot-probe scripts also accept
.B waitN
and
.B wait:N
frame waits.
.TP
.BI "--data-dir " path
Use
.I path
as the game-data root.
.TP
.B --scan-data
Scan game data and print found or missing required files, then exit.
.TP
.B --scan-game-data
Alias for
.BR --scan-data .
.TP
.BI "--game " id
Start a game directly. Valid IDs are
.BR dm1 ,
.BR csb ,
.BR dm2 ,
.BR nexus ,
and
.BR theron .
.TP
.B --menu
Show the startup menu even when a game was selected from the command line.
.TP
.B --fullscreen
Request fullscreen mode. This option is accepted by the current launcher CLI;
runtime wiring may vary by build.
.TP
.B --no-vsync
Disable vertical sync where supported. This option is accepted by the current
launcher CLI; runtime wiring may vary by build.
.TP
.B --fps
Show FPS where supported. This option is accepted by the current launcher CLI;
runtime wiring may vary by build.
.TP
.B --retroachievements
Enable the RetroAchievements runtime bridge.
.TP
.BI "--ra-user " name
Set RetroAchievements username for this run.
.TP
.BI "--ra-token " token
Set RetroAchievements API token for this run. Avoid placing tokens in shell
history on shared systems.
.TP
.BI "--ra-hardcore " "0|1"
Set RetroAchievements hardcore mode for this run.
.TP
.B --version
Print Firestaff version and exit.
.TP
.BR "--help" ", " "-h"
Print command-line help and exit.
.SH BOOT PROBE OPTIONS
Boot-probe options are mainly for tests and packaging verification. They start
the selected game, inspect the boot receipt, and fail when expectations do not
match.
.TP
.B --boot-probe
Enable deterministic boot-probe mode. Requires
.BR --game .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-frames " n
Advance
.I n
idle frames before the probe receipt is inspected.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-phase " name
Fail unless the reported boot phase matches
.IR name .
.TP
.B --boot-probe-expect-runtime
Fail unless startup is inactive and a level is loaded.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-party " x,y,dir
Fail unless the party position and direction match.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-champions " n
Fail unless the champion count matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-level-loaded " "0|1"
Fail unless the level-loaded flag matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-asset-md5 " md5
Fail unless the boot asset MD5 matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-map " n
Fail unless the map or level index matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-runtime-tick-min " n
Fail unless the runtime tick is at least
.IR n .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-runtime-tick-max " n
Fail unless the runtime tick is at most
.IR n .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-startup-active " "0|1"
Fail unless the startup-active flag matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-startup-frame-min " n
Fail unless the startup frame is at least
.IR n .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-startup-frame-max " n
Fail unless the startup frame is at most
.IR n .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-startup-animation " id
Fail unless the startup/title animation ID matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-startup-animation-active " "0|1"
Fail unless the animation-active flag matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-title-frame-min " n
Fail unless the title frame is at least
.IR n .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-title-frame-max " n
Fail unless the title frame is at most
.IR n .
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-title-frame-boundary " n
Fail unless the title frame boundary matches.
.TP
.BI "--boot-probe-expect-title-ready " "0|1"
Fail unless the title-ready flag matches.
.SH LEGACY FRONTEND OPTIONS
Some builds also contain a legacy frontend parser used by older tooling. It
accepts:
.BR --v1 ,
.BR --v2 ,
.BR --v21 ,
.BR --v22 ,
.BR --windowed ,
.BR --scale ,
.BR --lang ,
.BR --data ,
.BR --saves ,
.BR --config ,
.BR --load ,
.BR --list-saves ,
.BR --headless ,
.BR --no-menu ,
.BR --validate ,
and
.BR "-V" .
.PP
Prefer the modern options above for normal Linux use.
.SH GAME DATA
Default data root:
.PP
.RS
.B ~/.firestaff/data/
.RE
.PP
Recommended layout:
.PP
.RS
.B ~/.firestaff/data/dm1/
.br
.B ~/.firestaff/data/csb/
.br
.B ~/.firestaff/data/dm2/
.br
.B ~/.firestaff/data/nexus/
.br
.B ~/.firestaff/data/theron/
.RE
.PP
Firestaff scans by hash and can find supported files in directories, ZIP-like
archives, ISO/BIN/IMG-style disc images, CUE sheets, TAR/TGZ/GZ, stored
LHA/LZH entries, CHD when
.B chdman
is installed, and several other archive or disk-image formats when suitable
local extraction tools are available.
.SH SAVEGAMES
Savegames and configuration are kept under the Firestaff user directory,
normally:
.PP
.RS
.B ~/.firestaff/
.RE
.PP
Game data and save data should be kept separate.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FIRESTAFF_DATA
Default game-data root when
.B --data-dir
is not supplied.
.TP
.B FS_ACCESSIBILITY
When set, enables the disk-backed accessibility/automation manifest at
.BR ~/.firestaff/accessibility.json .
.TP
.B SDL_VIDEODRIVER
Can be set to
.B dummy
for headless test runs.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Scan game data:
.B firestaff --scan-data
.TP
Start DM1 in original presentation:
.B firestaff --game dm1 --scale-mode 1
.TP
Use a custom game-data root:
.B firestaff --data-dir ~/Games/FirestaffData --scan-data
.TP
Start CSB directly:
.B firestaff csb
.TP
Run a short headless smoke:
.B SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy firestaff --duration 500 --game dm1
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.firestaff/data/
Default game-data directory.
.TP
.B ~/.firestaff/
Default Firestaff user directory for saves, configuration, cache, and runtime
state.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime or launch failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line argument or missing required boot-probe option.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL3 (7)
.PP
Project page:
